Below is the decomposition of the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, complete with goals and tasks structured in a tree format.

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                      | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation           | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food                    | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room.                      | -                            | Achieve   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Retrieval Capability  | Determine if the inpatient or a companion can retrieve the food.    | -                            | Query     | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Food to Table           | Place the food on the room table.                                    | FALLBACK(AT4, AT5)           | Perform   | G1       |
| G4      | Retrieve Food from Tray         | Ensure food is retrieved from the robot's tray by the inpatient or a helper. | FALLBACK(AT6, AT7, AT8)     | Achieve   | G1       |
| G5      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes           | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                 | FALLBACK(AT9, AT10, AT11)    | Achieve   | G1       |

#### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                  | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location             | Number of Robots |
| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Inpatient Room  | Move the robot to the designated inpatient room.                    | AND      | Hospital Room        | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Check Inpatient Record      | Access and analyze the inpatient record for retrieval capability info. | AND      | Hospital Database    | 1                |
| AT3     | Announce Meal Retrieval     | Indicate which meal should be retrieved by the inpatient.            | AND      | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT4     | Place Food on Table         | Physically place the food on the room table.                         | AND      | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT5     | Alert Incorrect Meal        | Notify if an incorrect meal is retrieved by the inpatient or helper. | AND      | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT6     | Inpatient Retrieves Meal    | Inpatient retrieves food from the robot's tray.                      | OR       | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT7     | Companion/Family Retrieves  | Companion/family retrieves food from the robot's tray.               | OR       | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT8     | Nurse/Robot Assists         | Nurse or another robot assists in retrieving food.                   | OR       | Hospital Room        | [1, 2]           |
| AT9     | Inpatient Retrieves Dishes  | Inpatient retrieves dirty dishes from the room.                     | OR       | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT10    | Companion/Family Retrieves  | Companion/family retrieves dirty dishes from the room.              | OR       | Hospital Room        | 1                |
| AT11    | Nurse/Robot Assists         | Nurse or another robot assists in retrieving dirty dishes.          | OR       | Hospital Room        | [1, 2]           |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G4, G5 [AND]**
  - **G2 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**
  - **G3 -> AT3, FALLBACK(AT4, AT5) [AND/OR]**
  - **G4 -> AT3, FALLBACK(AT6, AT7, AT8) [AND/OR]**
  - **G5 -> AT3, FALLBACK(AT9, AT10, AT11) [AND/OR]**

### Summary

The goal model represents the hierarchical decomposition of tasks required to successfully deliver food and retrieve dishes in a hospital setting. The model includes goals for determining retrieval capabilities, delivering food, retrieving food from the tray, and retrieving dirty dishes. Each goal is decomposed into tasks with specified locations and required robot numbers, ensuring that the system can handle various scenarios involving human-robot interaction and cooperation.
